vides biological and chemical compound sample exploration and management solutions for the life sciences industry in the United States, China, the United Kingdom, rest of Europe, the Asia Pacific, and internationally. It operates through Sample Management Solutions and Multiomics segments. The Sample Management Solutions segment provides sample management products and services, including automated stores, cryogenic systems, automated sample tubes, consumables and instruments, and controlled rate thawing devices, as well as sample repository services. This segment also offers consultation services to clients throughout their experimental design and implementation processes. The Multiomics segment provides genomic and other sample analysis services comprising gene sequencing, gene synthesis, and related services. The company was formerly known as Brooks Automation, Inc. and changed its name to Azenta, Inc. in December 2021. Azenta, Inc. was founded in 1978 and is headquartered in Burlington, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Martin D. Madaus D.V.M., Ph.D. | Interim President, CEO & Director | Age 65 | Compensation: $83,750 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Azenta, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.9B market cap on $622M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -2% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are contracting by -2.6pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at -2% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 39%.","The business throws off $27M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On 